Facts from other projects
-------------------------

Tuya does not publish its LAN protocol. The frame layouts, command
numbers, the 3.1 signature rule, the session key negotiation and the
discovery key this module uses are facts read from public descriptions,
chiefly tinytuya (github.com/jasonacox/tinytuya; MIT, Copyright (c) 2024
Jason Cox). No code was taken; see PROVENANCE.md. The bulb data point
layouts, colour formats and cover value schemes in dp.go are likewise
facts read from tinytuya's bulb and cover classes. The RGB and HSV
conversion in dp.go follows the algorithm of Python's colorsys module,
written anew in Go so its results match what tinytuya writes; no
Python code was copied.

The discovery key (UDPKey) is the MD5 digest of a short string that every
Tuya LAN implementation uses to read announcements; it is a public
protocol constant, not a credential and not a key of any device or
account.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile installs tinytuya 1.20.0 (MIT, Copyright (c)
2024 Jason Cox) and its dependencies from PyPI into a
python:3.12.10-slim image at test time (v0.1.0 ran on python:3.14-slim);
nothing of tinytuya is copied into this repository. interop/peer/device.py
and interop/peer/vectors.py are our own scripts that call tinytuya's
functions and classes.

